{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794236752,"nonce":"I3xsTGf5j8nEvr97NnPvUf1t4fc=","title":"Sidebar sizing and readable shortcut chords","message":"## Context\n- Expanded sidebar is 276 wide (`src/ui/screen.rs:28`) for four short labels; the longest, \"Repositories\", needs ~160.\n- Collapsed rail is 64 wide (`src/ui/screen.rs:29`) but nav icons are only 16 (`NAV_ICON`, `src/ui/screen.rs:32`), so icons look small while the rail still eats space. The 32 gap between sidebar and page (`src/ui/screen.rs:50`) plus the 28 panel left padding (`src/ui/screen.rs:63`) add to it.\n- Mac chords render glued together, \"⌘K\" / \"⌘⇧L\" (`src/keymap.rs:208`), in tooltips (`src/ui/tooltip.rs:359` `tooltip_body`) and the help overlay (`src/ui/shortcuts.rs`, same table). Non-mac already uses \"Ctrl+K\".\n\n## Files\n- `src/ui/screen.rs:28-41` — `SIDEBAR_WIDTH`, `RAIL_WIDTH`, `NAV_ICON`, `nav_icon_pad`\n- `src/ui/screen.rs:50`, `:59-64` — sidebar/page gap and panel padding\n- `src/ui/screen.rs:216-268` — `sidebar`\n- `src/ui/screen.rs:1122-1132` — rail centering tests\n- `src/keymap.rs:196-211` — `Chord::render`; tests `src/keymap.rs:453`, `:460`, `:484`\n\n## Approach\n- `SIDEBAR_WIDTH` 276 → 200; `RAIL_WIDTH` 64 → 56; `NAV_ICON` 16 → 20. `nav_icon_pad` already derives centering from these, so keep using it.\n- Sidebar/page gap 32 → 20; leave panel padding unless the rail still reads wide after that.\n- Mac render joins parts with \"+\": \"⌘+K\", \"⌘+⇧+L\", matching the existing \"Ctrl+Shift+L\" style. Plain keys (\"?\", \"Esc\") unchanged.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Keycap-style pill rendering for chords.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Expanded sidebar is 200 wide with no label clipped; collapsed rail is 56 wide with 20px icons\n- Existing rail-centering tests pass with the new constants\n- `keymap` tests expect \"⌘+K\" and \"⌘+⇧+L\" on mac; tooltips and the help overlay show the separated form\n- `cargo test`, clippy and fmt gates pass","files":null}]}